## Environment

Python 3.11; numpy 2.4.6, scipy 1.17.1, pandas 3.0.6, scikit-learn 1.9.1, torch 2.14.1 (CPU build), joblib 1.6.0, pyarrow 26.0.0 (`requirements.txt`). No GPU. The scripts set `OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=OMP_NUM_THREADS=MKL_NUM_THREADS=1`; keep BLAS single-threaded (multi-threaded BLAS made the small eigen-decompositions 10× slower on a shared machine). Peak memory of one worker < 6 GB.

## Data

`scripts/00_download.sh` downloads the 13 score matrices and model lists from a public repository at a pinned commit (`55faff496947789f94e6b5908c77cbc3e84f81ad` of `socialfoundations/benchmark-prediction`; ~80 MB) into `data/raw/` and writes `SHA256SUMS`. The data are **not** bundled here. Only the binary item-level outcomes (and model names, used to derive families) are used; no benchmark text, no code of that repository. The source repository states an MIT licence; the licences of the benchmark datasets whose outcomes the matrices record (Open LLM Leaderboard v2 tasks, HELM scenarios) were not individually verified, which is one reason the matrices are fetched rather than redistributed. `python3 scripts/01_audit.py` writes the audit (`results/audit.csv`): models, duplicates dropped, constant items, families.

## Run

```
bash scripts/00_download.sh
python3 -I scripts/01_audit.py
bash scripts/run_all.sh 8            # 8 worker processes; all experiments and analyses, writes results/raw*/ and results/*.csv
```

`SKIP="extra inner50 kmstrong highR" bash scripts/run_all.sh 8` leaves out stages (`main variants msrc 2pct extra inner50 kmstrong highR analyze`). Step by step: `python3 -I scripts/02_run.py BENCH SPLIT --draws 10 --d 2 --out results/raw` runs one (benchmark, split) cell (`BENCH` ∈ the 13 names, `SPLIT` ∈ `interp lineage extrap extrap10 extrap50`; `--ngrid N` runs a single budget, `--designs`, `--no-cat`, `--msrc M`, `--extra`, `--inner-frac F`, `--tag`: see the header of the script); then `03_analyze.py`, `04_msrc.py`, `05_bands.py`, `06_select.py`, `09_paired.py` (paired inner-split comparison, `results/inner50/paired_vs_main.csv`), `10_ceiling_centred.py` and `11_extrap_bias.py` (checks of two explanations; `results/ceiling_centred.csv`, `results/extrap_bias.csv`; usage in their headers). `scripts/pilot_d.py` is the source-only pilot that fixed the latent dimension d = 2 (`results/pilot_d.csv`).

Seeds: `BASE_SEED = 20261126` combined with the tuple (benchmark, split, fold, n, draw, design index); fold assignment uses seed 0; bootstraps use fixed seeds in the scripts. Reproducibility across machines (other CPU, other BLAS) was not tested; small floating-point differences in individual predictions are possible.

Compute (single-threaded workers on a shared machine; hours are the wall-clock time of each job measured in the runner, an upper bound of its CPU time): main runs (38 jobs) 3.3 hours; sensitivity splits `extrap10`/`extrap50` (26 jobs) 1.4; source-count (`--msrc`), 2 % budget, extra estimators, larger-gap inner split, strong k-means (7 benchmarks only) and the 100-draw run: stage table with hours in `REPRODUCE.md`. The largest cells are `mmlu_pro`, `bbh`, `openllm_math` (up to ~25 min per cell at the main runs).

